H5700.definition:
from H5695 (עֵגֶל); vituline;
Eglon, the name of a place in Palestine and of a Moabitish king
KJV: Eglon.

H5701.definition:
a primitive root;
to be sad
KJV: grieve.

H5702.definition:
a primitive root;
to debar, i.e. from marriage
KJV: stay.

H5703.definition:
from H5710 (עָדָה);
properly, a (peremptory) terminus, i.e. (by implication) duration, in the sense of advance or perpetuity (substantially as a noun, either with or without a preposition)
KJV: eternity, ever(-lasting, -more), old, perpetually, [phrase] world without end.

H5704.definition:
properly, the same as H5703 (עַד) (used as a preposition, adverb or conjunction; especially with a preposition);
as far (or long, or much) as, whether of space (even unto) or time (during, while, until) or degree (equally with)
KJV: against, and, as, at, before, by (that), even (to), for(-asmuch as), (hither-) to, [phrase] how long, into, as long (much) as, (so) that, till, toward, until, when, while, ([phrase] as) yet.

H5705.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5704 (עַד)
{as far (or long, or much) as, whether of space (even unto) or time (during, while, until) or degree (equally with)}
KJV: [idiom] and, at, for, (hither-) to, on till, (un-) to, until, within.

H5706.definition:
the same as H5703 (עַד) in the sense of the aim of an attack;
booty
KJV: prey.

H5707.definition:
contracted from H5749 (עוּד);
concretely, a witness; abstractly, testimony; specifically, a recorder, i.e. prince
KJV: witness.

H5708.definition:
from an unused root meaning to set a period (compare H5710 (עָדָה), H5749 (עוּד));
the menstrual flux (as periodical); by implication (in plural) soiling
KJV: filthy.

H5709.definition:
(Aramaic) or עֲדָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H5710 (עָדָה)
{to advance, i.e. pass on or continue; causatively, to remove; specifically, to bedeck (i.e. bring an ornament upon)}
KJV: alter, depart, pass (away), remove, take (away).

H5710.definition:
a primitive root;
to advance, i.e. pass on or continue; causatively, to remove; specifically, to bedeck (i.e. bring an ornament upon)
KJV: adorn, deck (self), pass by, take away.

H5711.definition:
from H5710 (עָדָה); ornament;
Adah, the name of two women
KJV: Adah.

H5712.definition:
feminine of H5707 (עֵד) in the original sense of fixture;
a stated assemblage (specifically, a concourse, or generally, a family or crowd)
KJV: assembly, company, congregation, multitude, people, swarm. Compare H5713 (עֵדָה).

H5713.definition:
feminine of H5707 (עֵד) in its techn. sense;
testimony
KJV: testimony, witness. Compare H5712 (עֵדָה).

H5714.definition:
or עִדּוֹא; or עִדִּיא; from H5710 (עָדָה); timely;
Iddo (or Iddi), the name of five Israelites
KJV: Iddo. Compare H3035 (יִדּוֹ), H3260 (יֶעְדִּי).

H5715.definition:
feminine of H5707 (עֵד);
testimony
KJV: testimony, witness.

H5716.definition:
from H5710 (עָדָה) in the sense of trappings;
finery; generally an outfit; specifically, a headstall
KJV: [idiom] excellent, mouth, ornament.

H5717.definition:
from H5716 (עֲדִי) and H410 (אֵל); ornament of God;
Adiel, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Adiel.

H5718.definition:
or עֲדָיָהוּ; from H5710 (עָדָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has adorned;
Adajah, the name of eight Israelites
KJV: Adaiah.

H5719.definition:
from H5727 (עָדַן);
voluptuous
KJV: given to pleasures.

H5720.definition:
the same as H5719 (עָדִין);
Adin, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Adin.

H5721.definition:
from H5719 (עָדִין); effeminacy;
Adina, an Israelite
KJV: Adina.

H5722.definition:
probably from H5719 (עָדִין) in the original sense of slender (i.e. a spear);
