KJV: Eden.

H5730.definition:
or (feminine) עֶדְנָה; from H5727 (עָדַן);
pleasure
KJV: delicate, delight, pleasure. See also H1040 (בֵּית עֵדֶן).

H5731.definition:
the same as H5730 (עֵדֶן) (masculine);
Eden, the region of Adam's home
KJV: Eden.

H5732.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of H5708 (עֵד);
a set time; technically, a year
KJV: time.

H5733.definition:
from H5727 (עָדַן); pleasure;
Adna, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Adna.

H5734.definition:
from H5727 (עָדַן); pleasure;
Adnah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Adnah.

H5735.definition:
from H5712 (עֵדָה); festival;
Adadah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Adadah.

H5736.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, have) redundant
KJV: be more, odd number, be (have) over (and above), overplus, remain.

H5737.definition:
a primitive root;
to arrange as a battle, a vineyard (to hoe); hence, to muster and so to miss (or find wanting)
KJV: dig, fail, keep (rank), lack.

H5738.definition:
from H5737 (עֲדַר); an arrangement (i.e. drove);
Eder, an Israelite
KJV: Ader.

H5739.definition:
from H5737 (עֲדַר);
an arrangement, i.e. muster (of animals)
KJV: drove, flock, herd.

H5740.definition:
the same as H5739 (עֵדֶר);
Eder, the name of an Israelite and of two places in Palestine
KJV: Edar, Eder.

H5741.definition:
from H5739 (עֵדֶר) and H410 (אֵל); flock of God;
Adriel, an Israelite
KJV: Adriel.

H5742.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
a lentil
KJV: lentile.

H5743.definition:
a primitive root;
to be dense or dark, i.e. to becloud
KJV: cover with a cloud.

H5744.definition:
