Avvith (or Avvoth), a place in Palestine
KJV: Avith.

H5763.definition:
a primitive root;
to suckle, i.e. give milk
KJV: milch, (ewe great) with young.

H5764.definition:
from H5763 (עוּל);
a babe
KJV: sucking child, infant.

H5765.definition:
a primitive root;
to distort (morally)
KJV: deal unjustly, unrighteous.

H5766.definition:
or עָוֶל; and (feminine) עַוְלָה; or עוֹלָה; or עֹלָה; from H5765 (עֲוַל);
(moral) evil
KJV: iniquity, perverseness, unjust(-ly), unrighteousness(-ly); wicked(-ness).

H5767.definition:
intensive from H5765 (עֲוַל);
evil (morally)
KJV: unjust, unrighteous, wicked.

H5768.definition:
or עֹלָל; from H5763 (עוּל);
a suckling
KJV: babe, (young) child, infant, little one.

H5769.definition:
or עֹלָם; from H5956 (עָלַם);
properly, concealed, i.e. the vanishing point; generally, time out of mind (past or future), i.e. (practically) eternity; frequentatively, adverbial (especially with prepositional prefix) always
KJV: alway(-s), ancient (time), any more, continuance, eternal, (for, (n-)) ever(-lasting, -more, of old), lasting, long (time), (of) old (time), perpetual, at any time, (beginning of the) world ([phrase] without end). Compare H5331 (נֶצַח), H5703 (עַד).

H5770.definition:
