H5782.definition:
a primitive root (rather identical with through the idea of opening the eyes);
to wake (literally or figuratively)
KJV: (a-) wake(-n, up), lift up (self), [idiom] master, raise (up), stir up (self).

H5783.definition:
a primitive root;
to (be) bare
KJV: be made naked.

H5785.definition:
from H5783 (עוּר);
skin (as naked); by implication, hide, leather
KJV: hide, leather, skin.

H5786.definition:
a primitive root (rather denominatively from H5785 (עוֹר) through the idea of a film over the eyes);
to blind
KJV: blind, put out. See also H5895 (עַיִר).

H5787.definition:
intensive from H5786 (עָוַר);
